<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mahmud Shah Durrani</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1769">1769</a>–<a href="/years/1829">1829</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mahmud Shah <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/durrani-empire">Durrani</a> was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sadozai">Sadozai</a> ruler of the Durrani Empire, reigning in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kabul">Kabul</a> from 1801 to 1803 and again from 1809 to 1818. When the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barakzai-dynasty">Barakzai</a> brothers took over most of the realm, he withdrew to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herat">Herat</a>, which he and his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kamran-shah-durrani">Kamran Shah</a> held as an independent principality. He died there in 1829.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mahmud-shah-durrani.jpg" alt="Mahmud Shah Durrani" width="200" height="309" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shah_Mahmud.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
